CPENT Challenge 63 — Notes

Question: What Nmap script argument should be specified before the domain to enumerate Kerberos users?

Objective: Identify valid usernames in the LPT.COM Active Directory domain using Nmap.

1. Command
echo "administrator" > /tmp/test-user.txt
sudo nmap -p 88 --script krb5-enum-users \
--script-args krb5-enum-users.realm=LPT.COM,userdb=/tmp/test-user.txt \
172.25.170.190
2. Command explanation

Parameter

	

Purpose




-p 88

	

Scans the Kerberos port




--script krb5-enum-users

	

Runs the Kerberos user enumeration script




krb5-enum-users.realm=LPT.COM

	

Specifies the Kerberos realm




userdb=/tmp/test-user.txt

	

Provides the username wordlist




172.25.170.190

	

Target IP address

